WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.083
How does a gene become a trait?

2
00:00:01.083 --> 00:00:04.694
Follow one feather colour, from DNA to the bird you see.

3
00:00:04.694 --> 00:00:08.028
DNA is a long code. A gene is one section of it.

4
00:00:08.028 --> 00:00:11.361
A gene is the instructions for making a protein.

5
00:00:11.361 --> 00:00:14.694
Genes come in versions called alleles. You get one from each parent.

6
00:00:14.694 --> 00:00:18.028
Here D = dark feathers (dominant) and d = pale feathers (recessive).

7
00:00:18.028 --> 00:00:22.472
The alleles decide the proteins, and the proteins make the trait.

8
00:00:22.472 --> 00:00:25.250
Cross two Dd parents in a Punnett square.

9
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.583
DD, Dd, Dd, dd: a 3 in 4 chance of dark and 1 in 4 of pale.

10
00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:31.361
Genotype is the alleles. Phenotype is what you see.

11
00:00:31.361 --> 00:00:35.836
Define gene and allele, then show the cross. Give the ratio.

12
00:00:35.806 --> 00:00:40.750
